    <string name="privacy_policy_device_title">Data on this device</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_device_body">Pole parkla stores your profile, recipient, reports, templates, photos and local plate-crop coordinates in the app’s private storage. There are no analytics, ads or background sync, and Android backup is disabled.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_location_title">Location and maps</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_location_body">When a report has foreground or photo metadata coordinates, Pole parkla automatically sends the exact point over HTTPS to Maa- ja Ruumiamet’s In-AKS service to suggest nearby addresses. Opening the map loads OpenFreeMap tiles and exposes the device IP address and viewed area to that service. Photos, registration number, profile, recipient and letter text are not sent to In-AKS or OpenFreeMap.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_cloud_title">Optional cloud recognition</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_cloud_body">On-device recognition is automatic and offline. Cloud recognition runs only after provider-specific consent and sends one EXIF-free primary JPEG to the configured Workers AI or OpenAI provider. Profile, address, coordinates, other photos and letter text are not included.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_mail_title">Mail and deletion</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_mail_body">Pole parkla prepares a draft and attachments, then opens your selected mail app; it does not send the message itself. The mail app controls editing and sending. Delete all local data removes reports, photos, settings, tokens, temporary copies and address and map caches.</string>
